    "q-177652": {
      "dom_id": "step-q177652",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Let $I=[-1,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [-|i|,|i|].$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=-0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{-0.5}=\\{-0.5\\}\\times [-0.5,0.5]=\\{(-0.5,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [-0.5,0.5]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(-0.5,-0.5)$ to the point $(-0.5,0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14242415/assets/b7793d85e02ccd05c55c34971c90be087d58274eabd21f46fe09f08ccd60797b.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [-|i|,|i|]=\\{(i,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [-|i|,|i|]\\}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,-|i|)$ to the point $(i,|i|).$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14242415/assets/c30712295adfe51c655662cc09f8f1e23b3ea97573693154e0e0b6ba48e15c07.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following figure that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14242415/assets/8ce0c60aafe1a41b372c1f1477241c584d6f8ae224113c360576feb37fc25a8c.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
