    "q-175302": {
      "dom_id": "step-q175302",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "Let $I=[1,2]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,2-i]\\times \\{i\\}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}=[0,2-1]\\times \\{1\\}=[0,1]\\times \\{1\\}=\\{(k,1)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(0,1)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14242415/assets/ddb7039dfcdbc2ef4070ce732c635a48194b6675cc3c78de6267e656c5e8387a.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,2-i]\\times \\{i\\}=\\{(k,i)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,2-i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(0,i)$ to the point $(2-i,i).$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14242415/assets/e83644a2f0de96ee58ea893028bb7a42681ee71a15d194f2b344c4c15f60fafe.png)\n\nThere are no points that lie in all sets. Therefore, the intersection of the indexed sets is $∅,$ the empty set.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
